  arbitrary opaque values are rejected. Returns `{:vector v, :provenance [[pc origin root\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linearize.cljc:367:   `[:source medium batch-token j]`; the member index is the selected\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linearize.cljc:370:  [{:yin/keys [source-medium batch-token batch root\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linearize.cljc:371:               source-positions frontend-metadata entity-occurrences]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linearize.cljc:379:  (let [origin (vm/source-origin source-medium batch-token root)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linearize.cljc:382:           :source-positions (or source-positions [])\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linearize.cljc:389:   operands are opaque: a literal map shaped like a node is not a node.\"\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linearize.cljc:395:    :if [(:test node) (:consequent node) (:alternate node)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linearize.cljc:397:    (:stream/cursor :stream/next :stream/close) [(:source node)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linearize.cljc:407:   (doseq [node (tree-seq map? ast-children ast)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linearize.cljc:418:   Successive batches on one medium are independent AST programs whose\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:16:   globals, registration, or discovery, and the source stream never enters\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:19:  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:27:  \"Internal not-found sentinel used to verify :present read-backs. An opaque\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:29:   legal opaque payload, and a keyword sentinel would be ambiguous with a\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:47:   byte for byte — space-separated sequential elements, `, `-separated map\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:50:   set prints through its metadata-less seq on Dart). Scalars still print\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:71:          (sequential? n)\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:78:  \"Normalize a value so equal values print identically: maps and sets sort by\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:79:   canonically-printed key/element, sequences recurse, and collection metadata is\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:91:   record and its equal plain map would collide somewhere. order-normalize\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:102:                            ;; readers stamp source coordinates onto list\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:103:                            ;; literals, which would make an address depend\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:111:                        (if (seq m)\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:138:          ;; lists and seqs are one canonical value: = calls them equal and\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:143:          (sequential? v) (attach-meta\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:212:                   high-bits (quot bit-len 0x100000000)\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:337:  \"Mint the content-addressed key for an opaque payload, derived solely from\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:378:     :present  — an equal value is already stored under that address.\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:386:   address, not just with =, which ignores it. Equal content is idempotent\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:394:      (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing handle requires :put-content-fn\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:397:      (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing handle requires :get-content-fn\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:426:  \"Retrieve the opaque value stored at a content address.\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:437:      (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing handle requires :get-content-fn\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:460:   members is a sequence of {:stream <dao.stream reader handle> :cursor\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:461:   <opaque>} entries. The composition mints each cursor itself, from an\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:481:                               \"dao.jing pool member requires a cursor minted by its stream\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing.cljc:485:                               \"dao.jing pool member requires a dao.stream reader\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:1:(ns dao.space.query\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:2:  \"The reader-side index consumer (docs/design/dao.space.query.md).\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:5:   Datalog `q` and `pull` above them, with `current` and `history` as the\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc:20:  (:require [dao.datom :as datom]\nsr