nonical de Bruijn projection of the named Universal AST\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:8:pipeline is:\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:11:Yang -> named Universal AST -> de Bruijn projection -> projected form\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:16:The named form remains the bijective, stored, queryable, and renderable form.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:17:The projected form is derived data for alpha-equivalence, hash identity, and\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:50:are excluded from projected identity. Input order and source tempids do not\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:57:and ignored; it is excluded from projected rows and hashes and does not make\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:106:Every child is projected under the scope at its occurrence. A lambda body is\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:107:projected after its frame is pushed; an application operator and operands share\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:112:The projection publishes a `:yin.debruijn/*` dimension descriptor, as required\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:114:hash domain separator. A projected semantic node is a content-addressed record\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:117:The descriptor declares the projected d5 semantic slots in this order:\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:118:`[:yin.debruijn/hash :yin.debruijn/type :yin.debruijn/arity\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:119::yin.debruijn/bound :yin.debruijn/free :yin.debruijn/value\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:120::yin.debruijn/op :yin.debruijn/key :yin.debruijn/prefix\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:121::yin.debruijn/buffer :yin.debruijn/parked-id :yin.debruijn/macro?\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:122::yin.debruijn/body :yin.debruijn/operator\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:123::yin.debruijn/operands :yin.debruijn/test :yin.debruijn/consequent\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debru